# Release signing for the Android build. Copy this file to `key.properties`
# beside it and fill the four values in. That copy is gitignored and must never
# be committed; neither must the keystore it names.
#
# Without it, a release build FAILS and prints these instructions. Debug and
# profile builds never read this file.
#
#   storeFile      absolute path to your keystore, which lives OUTSIDE this
#                  repository (a relative path resolves against
#                  app/android/app, which is inside it -- do not)
#   storePassword  the password of the keystore
#   keyAlias       the alias of the key inside it
#   keyPassword    the password of that key
#   storeType      optional, only if the keystore is not the JDK default format
#
# Create the keystore with keytool, from your JDK's bin directory:
#
#   keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore <path outside the repo>/<name>.jks \
#     -storetype JKS -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 -alias <alias>
#
# Back it up somewhere else. An installed Android app can only be updated by an
# artifact signed with the same key.
#
# The values below are empty on purpose. Filling this file in with anything
# that looks real is how a placeholder gets copied into a build.

storeFile=
storePassword=
keyAlias=
keyPassword=
